### What is the feature you are proposing?

Currently, `getContent` just returns the data in the static file. The problem with just returning the file data is that you lose metadata from the filesystem. 

In particular, you lose the modified timestamp, which makes caching mutable assets all but impossible. I ended up writing my own `cachingServeStatic` to get around this. I'm going to include it as a hopefully-useful example. My main goal here is to support sending a `LastModified` header along with the static file contents, and also to look at the browser's `IfModifiedSince` header and return a 304 if the file hasn't been modified. Without this, my static files were always resent on each request.

Here's my example. Note that this is impossible in the current `serveStatic` middleware since we no longer have access to the modified time (or the file size for that matter, so Hono doesn't send the `Content-Length` header either). I only support `Bun` since that's what I'm using in my project.

```typescript
import { getMimeType } from "hono/utils/mime";

import type { Env, MiddlewareHandler } from "hono";
import { join } from "node:path/posix";

export type ServeStaticOptions<E extends Env = Env> = {
  root?: string;
  path?: string;
}

export const cachingServeStatic = <E extends Env = Env>(
  options: ServeStaticOptions<E>
) : MiddlewareHandler => {
  const root = options.root ?? "./";

  return async (c, next) => {
    if (c.finalized) {
      return next();
    }

    if (c.req.method !== "GET" && c.req.method !== "HEAD") {
      return next();
    }

    let path: string;

    if (options.path) {
      path = options.path;

    } else {
      let filename: string;

      try {
        filename = decodeURIComponent(c.req.path)
        if (/(?:^|[\/\\])\.\.(?:$|[\/\\])/.test(filename)) {
          throw new Error()
        }
      } catch {
        return next()
      }

      path = join(root, filename);
    }

    const file = Bun.file(path);
    if (!file.exists) {
      return next();
    }

    const lastModified = file.lastModified;
    c.header("Last-Modified", new Date(lastModified).toUTCString());

    const size = file.size;
    c.header("Content-Length", size.toString());

    const type = getMimeType(path) || "application/octet-stream";
    c.header("Content-Type", type);

    const ifModifiedSince = c.req.header("If-Modified-Since");
    if (ifModifiedSince) {
      const ifModifiedSinceTime = new Date(ifModifiedSince).getTime();
      const modifiedTime = Math.floor(lastModified / 1000) * 1000; // Round down to the nearest second

      if (!isNaN(ifModifiedSinceTime) && modifiedTime <= ifModifiedSinceTime) {
        c.status(304);
        return c.body(null);
      }
    }

    c.status(200);
    if (c.req.method === "HEAD") {
      return c.body(null);
    }

    return c.body(await file.bytes());
  };
}
```

